## Copper sulfate
component-copper-sulfate = Copper sulfate
    .genitive = copper sulfate
component-copper-sulfate-decomposes-into = copper oxide (CuO) and sulfur oxides
component-copper-sulfate-electrolysis-note = Under current copper settles on the cathode (Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu), oxygen forms at the anode, and sulfuric acid stays in the solution: 2CuSO₄ + 2H₂O → 2Cu + O₂ + 2H₂SO₄. The solution slowly pales as the copper ions are used up.
component-copper-sulfate-description-novice = Bright blue crystals. A big blue crystal is easy to grow from its solution. Heated, the crystals lose water and turn white; a drop of water turns them blue again.
component-copper-sulfate-description-school = The blue colour comes from water molecules bound to copper ions (the pentahydrate CuSO₄·5H₂O). The solution conducts electricity; in electrolysis copper deposits on the cathode.
component-copper-sulfate-safety-school = Harmful if swallowed, irritates eyes and skin. Wear gloves and wash your hands.
component-copper-sulfate-model-notes = The enthalpy of solution is not checked against sources yet, so in the model dissolving does not change the temperature.
